<title>GERMANY: Brazil 97/98 coffee crop seen at 24-25.5 mln bags.</title>
<headline>Brazil 97/98 coffee crop seen at 24-25.5 mln bags.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop may total between 24 and 25.5 million bags compared with new estimates for 1996/97 of 30 million bags, German trader Bernhard Rothfos GmbH said in its quarterly digest.</p>
<p>&quot;The Brazil 96/97 crop, now coming to an end, has proved once more to be a surprise factor,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>&quot;With exports still running strong most sources agree to a larger crop than originally expected.&quot;</p>
<p>In an estimate published in January, Rothfos saw the 1996/97 Brazilian harvest at 27 million bags.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
